H2500.definition:
from H2498 (חָלַף);
properly, exchange; hence (as preposition) instead of
KJV: [idiom] for.

H2501.definition:
the same as H2500 (חֵלֶף); change;
Cheleph, a place in Palestine
KJV: Heleph.

H2502.definition:
a primitive root;
to pull off; hence (intensively) to strip, (reflex.) to depart; by implication, to deliver, equip (for fight); present, strengthen
KJV: arm (self), (go, ready) armed ([idiom] man, soldier), deliver, draw out, make fat, loose, (ready) prepared, put off, take away, withdraw self.

H2503.definition:
or חֵלֶץ; from H2502 (חָלַץ); perhaps, strength;
Chelets, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Helez.

H2504.definition:
from H2502 (חָלַץ) (in the sense of strength); only in the dual;
the loins (as the seat of vigor)
KJV: loins, reins.

H2505.definition:
a primitive root;
to be smooth (figuratively); by implication (as smooth stones were used for lots) to apportion or separate
KJV: deal, distribute, divide, flatter, give, (have, im-) part(-ner), take away a portion, receive, separate self, (be) smooth(-er).

H2506.definition:
from H2505 (חָלַק);
properly, smoothness (of the tongue); also an allotment
KJV: flattery, inheritance, part, [idiom] partake, portion.

H2507.definition:
the same as H2506 (חֵלֶק); portion;
Chelek, an Israelite
KJV: Helek.

H2508.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2505 (חָלַק);
a part
KJV: portion.

H2509.definition:
from H2505 (חָלַק);
smooth (especially of tongue)
KJV: flattering, smooth.

H2510.definition:
the same as H2509 (חָלָק); bare;
Chalak, a mountain of Idumaea
KJV: Halak.

H2513.definition:
feminine of H2506 (חֵלֶק);
properly, smoothness; figuratively, flattery; also an allotment
KJV: field, flattering(-ry), ground, parcel, part, piece of land (ground), plat, portion, slippery place, smooth (thing).

H2514.definition:
feminine from H2505 (חָלַק);
flattery
KJV: flattery.

H2515.definition:
feminine of H2512 (חַלֻּק);
a distribution
KJV: division.

H2516.definition:
patronymically from H2507 (חֵלֶק);
a Chelkite or descendant of Chelek
KJV: Helkites.

H2517.definition:
from H2505 (חָלַק); apportioned;
Chelkai, an Israelite
KJV: Helkai.

H2518.definition:
or חִלְקִיָּהוּ; from H2506 (חֵלֶק) and H3050 (יָהּ); portion of Jah;
Chilhijah, the name of eight Israelites
KJV: Hillkiah.

H2519.definition:
by reduplication from H2505 (חָלַק);
properly, something very smooth; i.e. a treacherous spot; figuratively, blandishment
KJV: flattery, slippery.

H2520.definition:
a form of H2513 (חֶלְקָה); smoothness;
Chelkath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Helkath.

H2521.definition:
from H2520 (חֶלְקַת) and the plural of H6697 (צוּר), with the article inserted; smoothness of the rocks;
Chelkath Hats-tsurim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Helkath-hazzurim.

H2522.definition:
a primitive root;
to prostrate; by implication, to overthrow, decay
KJV: discomfit, waste away, weaken.

H2524.definition:
from the same as H2346 (חוֹמָה);
a father-in-law (as in affinity)
KJV: father in law.

H2525.definition:
from H2552 (חָמַם);
hot
KJV: hot, warm.

H2526.definition:
the same as H2525 (חָם); hot (from the tropical habitat);
Cham, a son of Noah; also (as a patronymic) his descendants or their country
KJV: Ham.

H2527.definition:
from H2552 (חָמַם);
heat
KJV: heat, to be hot (warm).

H2528.definition:
(Aramaic) or חֲמָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H2534 (חֵמָה);
anger
KJV: fury.

H2529.definition:
or (shortened) חֵמָה; from the same root as H2346 (חוֹמָה);
curdled milk or cheese
KJV: butter.

H2530.definition:
a primitive root;
to delight in
KJV: beauty, greatly beloved, covet, delectable thing, ([idiom] great) delight, desire, goodly, lust, (be) pleasant (thing), precious (thing).

H2531.definition:
from H2530 (חָמַד);
delight
KJV: desirable, pleasant.

H2532.definition:
feminine of H2531 (חֶמֶד);
delight
KJV: desire, goodly, pleasant, precious.

H2533.definition:
from H2531 (חֶמֶד); pleasant;
