KJV: Hammon.

H2541.definition:
from H2556 (חָמֵץ);
properly, violent; by implication, a robber
KJV: oppressed.

H2542.definition:
from H2559 (חָמַק);
a wrapping, i.e. drawers
KJV: joints.

H2543.definition:
or (shortened) חֲמֹר; from H2560 (חָמַר);
a male ass (from its dun red)
KJV: (he) ass.

H2544.definition:
the same as H2543 (חֲמוֹר); donkey;
Chamor, a Canaanite
KJV: Hamor.

H2545.definition:
or (shortened) חֲמֹת; feminine of H2524 (חָם);
a mother-in-law
KJV: mother in law.

H2546.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning, to lie low;
a lizard (as creeping)
KJV: snail.

H2547.definition:
feminine of H2546 (חֹמֶט); low;
Chumtah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Humtah.

H2548.definition:
from H2556 (חָמֵץ);
seasoned, i.e. salt provender
KJV: clean.

H2549.definition:
or חֲמִשִּׁי; ordinal from H2568 (חָמֵשׁ);
fifth; also a fifth
KJV: fifth (part).

H2550.definition:
a primitive root;
to commiserate; by implication, to spare
KJV: have compassion, (have) pity, spare.

H2551.definition:
from H2550 (חָמַל);
commiseration
KJV: merciful, pity.

H2552.definition:
a primitive root;
to be hot (literally or figuratively)
KJV: enflame self, get (have) heat, be (wax) hot, (be, wax) warm (self, at).

H2553.definition:
from H2535 (חַמָּה);
