KJV: [idiom] pure, red wine.

H2562.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2561 (חֶמֶר);
wine
KJV: wine.

H2563.definition:
from H2560 (חָמַר);
properly, a bubbling up, i.e. of water, a wave; of earth, mire or clay (cement); also a heap; hence, a chomer or dry measure
KJV: clay, heap, homer, mire, motion.

H2564.definition:
from H2560 (חָמַר);
bitumen (as rising to the surface)
KJV: slime(-pit).

H2565.definition:
from H2560 (חָמַר) (compare H2563 (חֹמֶר));
a heap
KJV: heap.

H2566.definition:
from H2560 (חָמַר); red;
Chamran, an Idumaean
KJV: Amran.

H2567.definition:
a denominative from H2568 (חָמֵשׁ);
to tax a fifth
KJV: take up the fifth participle

H2568.definition:
masculine חֲמִשָּׁה; a primitive numeral;
five
KJV: fif(-teen), fifth, five ([idiom] apiece).

H2569.definition:
from H2567 (חָמַשׁ);
a fifth tax
KJV: fifth participle

H2570.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning, to be stout;
the abdomen (as obese)
KJV: fifth (rib).

H2571.definition:
passive participle of the same as H2570 (חֹמֶשׁ);
staunch, i.e. able-bodied soldiers
KJV: armed (men), harnessed.

H2572.definition:
multiple of H2568 (חָמֵשׁ);
fifty
KJV: fifty.

H2573.definition:
from the same as H2346 (חוֹמָה);
a skin bottle (as tied up)
KJV: bottle.

H2574.definition:
from the same as H2346 (חוֹמָה); walled;
Chamath, a place in Syria
KJV: Hamath, Hemath.

H2575.definition:
a variation for the first part of H2576 (חַמֹּת דֹּאר); hot springs;
Chammath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hammath.

H2576.definition:
from the plural of H2535 (חַמָּה) and H1756 (דּוֹר); hot springs of Dor;
Chammath-Dor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hamath-Dor.

H2577.definition:
patrial from H2574 (חֲמָת);
a Chamathite or native of Chamath
KJV: Hamathite.

H2578.definition:
from H2574 (חֲמָת) and H6678 (צוֹבָא); Chamath of Tsobah; probably the same as H2574 (חֲמָת)
Chamath-Tsobah
KJV: Hamath-Zobah.

H2580.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן);
graciousness, i.e. subjective (kindness, favor) or objective (beauty)
KJV: favour, grace(-ious), pleasant, precious, (well-) favoured.

H2581.definition:
the same as H2580 (חֵן); grace;
Chen, a figurative name for an Israelite
KJV: Hen.

H2582.definition:
probably from H2580 (חֵן) and H1908 (הֲדַד); favor of Hadad;
