KJV: Hannah.

H2585.definition:
from H2596 (חָנַךְ); initiated;
Chanok, an antediluvian patriach
KJV: Enoch.

H2586.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן); favored;
Chanun, the name of an Ammonite and of two Israelites
KJV: Hanun.

H2588.definition:
from H2583 (חָנָה);
properly, a vault or cell (with an arch); by implication, a prison
KJV: cabin.

H2589.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן) (in the sense of prayer);
supplication
KJV: be gracious, intreated.

H2590.definition:
a primitive root;
to spice; by implication, to embalm; also to ripen
KJV: embalm, put forth.

H2591.definition:
