wheat
KJV: wheat.

H2592.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן) and H410 (אֵל); favor of God;
Channiel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hanniel.

H2593.definition:
from H2596 (חָנַךְ);
initiated; i.e. practiced
KJV: trained.

H2595.definition:
from H2583 (חָנָה);
a lance (for thrusting, like pitching a tent)
KJV: javelin, spear.

H2597.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2598 (חֲנֻכָּה);
consecration
KJV: dedication.

H2598.definition:
from H2596 (חָנַךְ);
initiation, i.e. consecration
KJV: dedicating(-tion).

H2599.definition:
patronymically from H2585 (חֲנוֹךְ);
a Chanokite (collectively) or descendants of Chanok
KJV: Hanochites.
